-- time_cloud.fleet -- a fleet that takes the time from one member it enrols (TIME-1, STZ-OS-RULING-07).
--
-- A fleet's machines keep records that are ORDERED and UNDATED, and a fleet that wants dates names the one
-- member whose word about the time it takes: TIME_AUTHORITY. That member is enrolled like every other (its
-- KEY is the public half of the key it signs with), so what it signs is checked with a public key by anyone who
-- holds this file and no secret. The court judges what no machine can: that the authority's machine answers,
-- that the device that asks asks THAT address and port, takes THAT key's word, and has a way there (FR50-FR59).
--
-- KEY below is a placeholder, because a device makes its own key on its first boot and a file in a repository
-- cannot know it. experiment/os10_time.sh boots the authority, reads the public half it publishes and writes it
-- in a COPY of this file and of machines/time_till.machine -- which is what enrolment is.
--
-- HARDWARE says which physical unit each member is. Nothing on this wire serves addresses, so no register is
-- held against it; two machines on one wire need two different ones, and that is a fact about a deployment,
-- which belongs in a declaration and never in a script (HDW-1).

DEFINE FLEET nuage AS (
  LINK lan,
  TIME_AUTHORITY clockbox
) RATIONALE "Two machines on one wire that take the time of their records from the one that has a clock, and from nobody else"

DEFINE MEMBER clockbox AS (
  DECLARATION "time_clockbox.machine",
  KEY "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
  HARDWARE "52:54:00:12:36:01"
) RATIONALE "The time authority: the machine with the clock, enrolled so that what it signs can be checked"

DEFINE MEMBER till AS (
  DECLARATION "time_till.machine",
  HARDWARE "52:54:00:12:36:02"
) RATIONALE "The device that asks how late its record can be"
